/Title (docker stack deploy -c spark-swarm.yml sparkcluster  docker service ls  Interpretation:  Pulls the Spark image from Docker Hub, edits the YAML file to configure the cluster, and deploys it. `docker service ls` shows running Spark services. The cluster can be monitored via Spark UI at `http://192.168.162.130:8081`.  Step 6: Create Bioinformatics Classifier Script \(`bio_classifier.py`\):  from pyspark.sql import SparkSession  from pyspark.ml.feature import StringIndexer, VectorAssembler  from pyspark.ml.classification import LogisticRegression  from pyspark.ml.evaluation import MulticlassClassificationEvaluator)
